1222
00:55:47,950 --> 00:55:49,790
It's a very useful
debugging tool.

1223
00:55:49,790 --> 00:55:52,990
I hope you'll try it out
today and on Monday, maybe,

1224
00:55:52,990 --> 00:55:55,810
for the finger exercises
if you're having trouble.

1225
00:55:55,810 --> 00:55:59,350
And you can use it for
quizzes to help you debug.

1226
00:55:59,350 --> 00:56:00,700
But I can just show you.

1227
00:56:00,700 --> 00:56:03,740
It's pretty simple here because
it's just a step by step.

1228
00:56:03,740 --> 00:56:05,470
So we step through.

1229
00:56:05,470 --> 00:56:08,320
So the red says the line
I'm going to execute.

1230
00:56:08,320 --> 00:56:10,310
Green is the line
I just executed.

1231
00:56:10,310 --> 00:56:12,230
So I just executed meters 100.

1232
00:56:12,230 --> 00:56:16,120
So here I have my meters
variable with the value 100.

1233
00:56:16,120 --> 00:56:17,630
Step through next.

1234
00:56:17,630 --> 00:56:19,450
So I just executed
feet equals this.

1235
00:56:19,450 --> 00:56:24,770
So I now have a variable named
feet with a value 328.08.

1236
00:56:24,770 --> 00:56:26,590
Meters still 100.

1237
00:56:26,590 --> 00:56:33,760
And then meters 200,
feet remained 328.08.

1238
00:56:33,760 --> 00:56:35,710
So obviously, this is
a pretty simple program

1239
00:56:35,710 --> 00:56:37,240
to run the Python
Tutor on, but you

1240
00:56:37,240 --> 00:56:44,500
can imagine using it in
more complex settings.

1241
00:56:44,500 --> 00:56:45,700
How about one more?

1242
00:56:45,700 --> 00:56:47,770
And this is my last example.

1243
00:56:47,770 --> 00:56:49,990
I want you to try to
write a program that

1244
00:56:49,990 --> 00:56:51,910
swaps the values of x and y.

1245
00:56:51,910 --> 00:56:53,800
So originally--
and I'll draw this,

1246
00:56:53,800 --> 00:56:55,610
the memory diagram real quick.

1247
00:56:55,610 --> 00:56:58,330
So we have-- this is our memory.

1248
00:56:58,330 --> 00:57:00,970
We have x is bound to 1.

1249
00:57:00,970 --> 00:57:03,550
Y is bound to 2.

1250
00:57:03,550 --> 00:57:08,110
And what I want to do
without saying x equals 2,

1251
00:57:08,110 --> 00:57:10,750
y equals 1, what I want
to do is swap the values.

1252
00:57:10,750 --> 00:57:14,980
I want x to be associated with
